            0.522,
            0.886,
            0.582
          ],
          "content": "2. The parallel sides of a trapezium are 40 cm and 20 cm. If its non-parallel sides are both equal, each being 26 cm, find the area of the trapezium."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.588,
            0.885,
            0.63
          ],
          "content": "3. Find the area of a triangle, given that its sides are 8 cm and 11 cm long, and its perimeter is 32 cm."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.131,
            0.635,
            0.885,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": "4. The sides of a triangular plot are in the ratio 3: 5: 7; its perimeter is 300 m. Find its area."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.682,
            0.885,
            0.724
          ],
          "content": "5. One diagonal of a rhombus is twice as long as the other diagonal. If the rhombus has area 128 cm<sup>2</sup>, find the length of the shorter diagonal."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.73,
            0.883,
            0.771
          ],
          "content": "6. ABCD is a parallelogram. P and Q are any two points on side AB. What can you say about the ratio area (∆PCD): area (∆QCD)?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.132,
            0.776,
            0.885,
            0.818
          ],
          "content": "7. O is any point on the diagonal PR of a parallelogram PQRS. Prove that the areas of triangles PSO and PQO are equal."
        },
        {
